## Practical Example: Payment Processing System

Let’s build a small system that processes different types of payments:
- Credit cards
- PayPal
- Cryptocurrency

We’ll use an interface to define the contract for all payment methods.

```csharp
public interface IPaymentProcessor
{
    bool ProcessPayment(decimal amount);
    string GetPaymentMethodName();
}
```

Now, implement it:

```csharp
public class CreditCardProcessor : IPaymentProcessor
{
    public bool ProcessPayment(decimal amount)
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"Processing credit card payment of ${amount}...");
        // Simulate success
        return true;
    }

    public string GetPaymentMethodName()
    {
        return "Credit Card";
    }
}

public class PayPalProcessor : IPaymentProcessor
{
    public bool ProcessPayment(decimal amount)
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"Processing PayPal payment of ${amount}...");
        // Simulate success
        return true;
    }

    public string GetPaymentMethodName()
    {
        return "PayPal";
    }
}

public class CryptoProcessor : IPaymentProcessor
{
    public bool ProcessPayment(decimal amount)
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"Processing crypto payment of ${amount}...");
        // Simulate success
        return true;
    }

    public string GetPaymentMethodName()
    {
        return "Bitcoin";
    }
}
```

Now, write a method that works with *any* payment processor:

```csharp
public void Checkout(IPaymentProcessor processor, decimal amount)
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Starting payment with {processor.GetPaymentMethodName()}...");
    bool success = processor.ProcessPayment(amount);
    Console.WriteLine(success ? "Payment successful!" : "Payment failed.");
}
```

Use it:

